-- title:
--   Descent of level automorphisms to the level field, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ as intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be an intermediate field over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be finite over $k_0$, and let $A_1$ be a valuation subring of $K_1$. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ such that (i) $k_0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})\sqcup F_0=\top$, (ii) $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\zeta'$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, (iii) for every $K'$ finite over $k_0$, any family $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and any $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with all $a_i$ in $T':=k_0(\text{image of }K')\sqcup F_0$ and $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ has all $a_i=0$, and (iv) every element whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb` (rational coefficients) belongs to $F_0$: setting $T_1:=k_0(\text{image of }K_1)\sqcup F_0$, for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is the inclusion $K_1\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and every $j_1\in T_1$ mapping to the image of `coeffEmb` applied to `jq`, there exists $j'\in T_1$ whose Laurent series is `coeffEmb` of `qExpand ℚ q jq` (the $q$-expansion of $j$ with exponents multiplied by $q$), such that $j'$ lies in `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₁ T₁ j₁`, $j_1$ lies in `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₁ T₁ j'`, and every $g$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ generated by the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ admits an $A_1$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $T_1$ with: $\sigma$ and $\sigma^{-1}$ agree with $g$ and $g^{-1}$ on $T_1$, $\sigma(j')=j'$, $\sigma$ preserves membership in `chartAlgFin A₁ T₁ j₁` and in `chartAlgInf A₁ T₁ j'` in both directions, and for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (a valuation subring containing the constants, proper, with principal ideals) which is rational, i.e. $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ surjects onto its residue field, the translate $g\cdot P$ is rational and satisfies $(g\cdot P).\mathrm{evalAt}(g f)=P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ and $g f\in (g\cdot P)$'s valuation subring iff $f\in P$'s, for all $f$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ instance of the statement that the group generated by the level automorphisms of the full-level modular function field descends to the $A_1$-form $T_1$ of that field, fixing the function with $q$-expansion $j(q^q)$ and preserving the two chart algebras of the associated two-chart integral model, while acting compatibly on rational places. It feeds the Igusa-tower leg of the semistable-covering argument, being used in the comparison of Igusa rings and in the constructions of level-automorphism translates of centred points on the two-chart integral model.
